                "retweet_count": 172,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "This week @USDA proposed common-sense changes to more than double the healthy eating opportunities for our most vulnerable populations by strengthening the stocking requirements for retailers participating in the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP). \n\nWe're seeking to raise the bar for stocking by: \n\u00a0\n\u25aa\ufe0fIncreasing variety requirements to seven per staple food category, more than DOUBLING the food choices required\n\u25aa\ufe0fClosing loopholes that allow certain snack foods to count as staple foods\n\u25aa\ufe0fSimplifying food classification, making standards easier for retailers to understand and @USDA_FNS to enforce\n\u00a0\nThese changes will reorient SNAP towards better nutrition and emphasizing whole, healthy food for program participants. \n\nWith the help of Dr. @RealBenCarson, who was officially sworn in this week as the USDA National Nutrition Advisor, we are delivering on @POTUS\u2019s promise to turn the tide on chronic disease and MAKE AMERICA HEALTHY AGAIN! \ud83e\udd57",
